Z||000002||Doni Hagan||09-13-2001||12:47 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by cadaver:<BR><B>You have sent it to me twice and your email is no bueno. And I have your money order what should I do with it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I recently found out about the file being sent around. I don't know how it's happening but I DIDN'T SEND IT! It's been sent to my home e-mail address as well as my wife's. There's no way I'd e-mail MYSELF from my own office. All I can figure is it's gotten into my address book and is going down the <BR>F#%$ing list. At least 12 people have received it and I DIDN'T SEND IT!<P>I've entered a post warning members of the file however, I'll repeat some of it here. <P>If you get an e-mail titled "DONI'S FIERO FILE" asking for advise DON'T OPEN IT!!!  DELETE IT IMMEDIATELY!!! Honest to God, I didn't send it. The techie at the studio is going to get to the bottom of this tomorrow. <P>BTW, the link suggested by 007Doug will work to get rid of it. You may have to run it while in SAFE MODE but it WILL get rid of it. Again, I'm really sorry about this and sincerely apologise for the PITA it may have caused anyone.  <P>RE: The money order. It would be greatly appreciated if you would send it back to my offices. I believe there's a return address on the envelope. I'll reimburse you for the stamp, if necessary. Thanks, Tom and sorry for the inconvenience.   <P><p>[This message has been edited by Doni Hagan (edited 09-13-2001).]||||reg||9
